# Bundled stdlib manifest -- the single source of truth for which
# namespaces are baked into the binary as C string literals.
#
# One line per bundled namespace. Columns are whitespace-separated:
#
#   1. source path, relative to the repo root (lib/.../<name>.clj)
#   2. capability group the namespace belongs to (documentation only;
#      the authoritative capability gating lives in the hand-written
#      src/prim/install_stdlib.c, which is the public embedder API)
#
# Both bundlers derive everything else from column 1:
#
#   namespace  lib/clojure/core/async.clj -> clojure.core.async
#              (drop lib/, drop .clj, slashes become dots)
#   c-symbol   lib/clojure/core/async.clj -> lib_clojure_core_async
#              (drop .clj, non-alphanumerics become underscores)
#
# The Makefile reads this file via $(shell) for the from-scratch
# bootstrap build; builtin.clj's bundled-stdlib parses the same file
# for the incremental `./mino task build`. src/core.clj is bundled
# too, but as core_mino by gen-core-header, not through this list.
#
# To add a bundled namespace: drop the .clj under lib/, add one line
# here, and add its deliberate mino_register_bundled_lib call in
# src/prim/install_stdlib.c. The cheap-lane parity test fails if the
# manifest and the C registration ever disagree.
#
# Lines beginning with # and blank lines are ignored.

lib/clojure/string.clj                  default
lib/clojure/set.clj                     default
lib/clojure/math.clj                    default
lib/clojure/walk.clj                    default
lib/clojure/edn.clj                     default
